Here's a PHP function that filters an array of user objects and returns only the active ones:

```php
<?php

/**
 * Filter an array of user objects, returning only active users.
 *
 * @param object[] $users Array of user objects with an `isActive` property.
 * @return object[] Array containing only active users (re-indexed).
 */
function getActiveUsers(array $users): array
{
    $activeUsers = array_filter($users, function ($user) {
        return isset($user->isActive) && $user->isActive === true;
    });

    // Re-index the array so keys are sequential (0, 1, 2, ...)
    return array_values($activeUsers);
}
```

### Example Usage

```php
