    ['name' => 'Laptop', 'price' => 999.99],
    ['name' => 'Mouse', 'price' => 19.99],
    ['name' => 'Keyboard', 'price' => 49.99],
];

$sortedProducts = sortProductsByPrice($products);
```

The result is ordered from lowest to highest price: Mouse, Keyboard, Laptop. Note that `usort()` reindexes the array’s numeric keys.

