## More robust version

Handles objects with either a property or a method, and lets you choose whether to re-index the result:

```php
<?php

/**
 * @param array<int|string, mixed> $users
 * @param bool $preserveKeys  Keep the original keys (true) or re-index (false)
 * @return array
 */
function getActiveUsers(array $users, bool $preserveKeys = true): array
{
    $active = array_filter($users, static function ($user): bool {
        if (!is_object($user)) {
            return false;
        }

        // 1) Method form: $user->isActive()
        if (method_exists($user, 'isActive')) {
            return (bool) $user->isActive();
        }

        // 2) Property form: $user->isActive / $user->active
        foreach (['isActive', 'active', 'is_active'] as $prop) {
            if (isset($user->$prop)) {
                return (bool) $user->$prop;
            }
        }

        return false;
    });

    return $preserveKeys ? $active : array_values($active);
}
```

**Example with objects**

